# Day 4 – Challenges

## Challenge 1 – LWC Not Appearing in App Builder

Initially, the placementHome component was not visible in Lightning App Builder.

### Solution

I checked the component metadata and ensured that the component was exposed using:

<isExposed>true</isExposed>

and that lightning__AppPage was included as a target.

After deploying the component to the correct Salesforce org, it appeared in Lightning App Builder.

## Challenge 2 – Deploying to the Correct Org

Multiple Salesforce orgs were connected to VS Code.

### Solution

I checked the connected orgs using:

sf org list

and verified the target org before deploying the LWC.

## Challenge 3 – Button and Welcome Message

The welcome message initially did not display as expected.

### Solution

I used a JavaScript property and event handler:

showWelcomeMessage()

The button calls the method using:

onclick={showWelcomeMessage}

## Challenge 4 – Application Status

I needed to change the application status after clicking a button.

### Solution

I created a JavaScript property:

applicationStatus = 'Not Applied';

and changed it to:

'Applied'

when the button was clicked.

## Engineering Lesson

Build incrementally and test each feature before moving to the next feature.
